WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.590
Although she's digitally rendered to look
alien, Proxima Midnight's voice and facial

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.080
structure are sure to make you ask yourself:
"Where do I know her from?"

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:13.480
Carrie Coon's convincingly intimidating motion-capture
performance in Infinity War is yet another

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.640
impressive addition to her acting résumé.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.100
Talk about a successful debut: For her very
first feature film appearance, Coon starred

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.220
alongside Ben Affleck in Gone Girl, the adaptation
of Gillian Flynn's twisted novel of the same

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:26.720
name.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.220
Coon starred as Margo Dunne, twin sister of
Affleck's leading man, Nick Dunne.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.380
She got the part by sending in an audition
tape, and she must've really knocked it out

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.820
of the park in order to get cast the old-fashioned
way.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.700
Coon really showcased the full range of her
acting chops, and it definitely had an effect

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.900
on the film's success.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.080
Gone Girl was a massive box office hit, bringing
in nearly $370 million worldwide.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.620
If the first movie you ever act in goes on
to become one of the top 20 highest-grossing

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.360
films of the year, you must be doing something
right.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:03.100
HBO's psychological mystery drama The Leftovers
focused on the lives of several people who

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.340
remained on Earth after two percent of the
entire global population vanished in a rapture-like

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:08.840
event.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.640
The series ran for three seasons and 28 episodes
from 2014 to 2017.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.220
Coon portrayed Nora Durst, a grieving widower
who lost both her husband and her children

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:19.760
in the event.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.600
She still views her work on the show with
great regard.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.810
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
she raved about how it affected her career,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:27.420
declaring:

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.860
"I rarely get recognized and whenever I do,
it has to do with The Leftovers because it

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.790
came into someone's life at a particularly
important time for them if they were dealing

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.200
with grief or loss or whatever tragedy and
they just caught it."

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.100
In the spring of 2017, Coon's acting career
really caught fire.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.220
While simultaneously shooting The Leftovers,
she also joined the cast of FX's smash hit

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.400
series Fargo for its third season.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.210
A black comedy wrapped up in a crime anthology,
the show is based on the Coen brothers' 1996

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.180
film of the same name.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.600
Coon starred as Gloria Burgle, the recently
divorced chief of police in snowy Eden Valley,

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.100
Minnesota.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.220
"Those are facts, and you at the heart of
the morass.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.840
What else am I supposed to see?"

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.560
Despite starring alongside such A-list actors
as Ewan McGregor and Mary Elizabeth Winstead,

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.360
Coon commanded viewers' attention, even earning
an Emmy nomination for Lead Actress in a Limited

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.620
Series or TV Movie.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.440
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
she opened up a bit about the "spring of Carrie

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.140
Coon," saying,

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.340
"Oh gosh, this year, this extraordinary year…

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.060
It's funny, I feel like I'm still processing
this year that I've had … I feel I’ve

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.280
been working nonstop for years now, and I
haven’t had time to take a breath."

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.600
It's generally considered a great honor to
work on a Steven Spielberg film, and Carrie

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.420
Coon is one of the lucky talents who can flaunt
that achievement on her IMDb page.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.360
In The Post, she portrayed journalist Meg
Greenfield, a proud member of the Washington

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.560
Post team responsible for publishing the Pentagon
Papers in 1971.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.490
The film, which also starred Tom Hanks and
Meryl Streep, brought in nearly $180 million

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.000
at the worldwide box office and nabbed two
Oscar nominations.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.720
Although her role was fairly minor, Coon's
time on set with an acclaimed director and

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:14.430
two of the biggest names in Hollywood history
is not an experience she will soon forget.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.420
She told Parade,

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.380
"The thing that I loved about working with
Meryl, Tom and Steven is that they all so

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.380
clearly still love what they're doing.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.360
They've been making films for decades and
it's still magical for them, still moving

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.620
for them, and important."

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.800
Steve McQueen's Widows featured an all-star
cast led by Viola Davis, Michelle Rodriguez,

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.680
Elizabeth Debicki, and Liam Neeson.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.740
And although her role was small, you can't
forget to include Carrie Coon on that list.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.940
The 2018 film follows four women forced to
embark on a heist after their gangster husbands

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:45.440
are killed.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.080
Coon plays Amanda, one of the widows who decides
not to partake in the plan.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.500
Although it garnered a decent amount of buzz
prior to its release, it ultimately didn't

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.420
fare too well at the box office, only earning
$76 million worldwide.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.600
In an interview with Observer, Coon dished
about her favorite parts of working on Widows,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.300
which was shot in her hometown of Chicago.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:11.080
She appreciated McQueen bringing his unique
point of view to a genre film, working alongside

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.400
greats such as Davis and Neeson, and getting
to sleep in her own bed for a change.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.120
In the acting world, you can't put a price
tag on working close to home.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.420
In the first season of USA's dark mystery
thriller The Sinner, Jessica Biel shined as

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.000
a woman coming to grips with the demons of
her past.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.840
For Season 2, the showrunners needed to find
a new leading lady to fill Biel's shoes.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.140
Although she wasn't their first choice, the
role of commune leader Vera Walker eventually

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:36.960
went to Coon.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.800
"She sneaks into your room at night and sits
on your chest.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.060
Have you ever been visited by her?"

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.190
The really interesting part of this story
is that Coon hadn't even intended to be on

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:49.940
the show at all.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.660
It was actually her husband, Pulitzer-Prize
winning playwright Tracy Letts, who received

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.100
the casting call for the role of Jack Novack.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.240
Since Coon had just delivered their first
child, she was looking forward to taking some

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.280
time off from acting.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.860
But when the role of Vera was reopened, they
offered it to Coon, and the rest is history.

